>> title: Butter Beans
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: beans, pork, southern, stew, side
>> counters: Meat and Three, One Pot
>> aka: lima beans, baby limas, large limas, butterbeans, speckled butter beans
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 40 min
>> slack: unforgiving — butter beans that stay whole and separate are undercooked; a few have to break up and thicken the pot before it is done
>> pairs-with: ham-hock-stock, skillet-cornbread, oxtails, collard-greens
>> washing-up: the Dutch oven
>> keeps: 4 days — they turn creamier as they sit, and the liquor sets to a light gel you stir back in warm

>> step: Cook these until a few of them break up and thicken the pot. The liquid goes creamy with no cream in it.
Cook these until a few of them break up and thicken the pot.

>> step: render 8 min
Render @salt pork{3%oz}(85 g; diced) in a #Dutch oven{} for ~render{8%min}.

>> step: sweat 6 min
Sweat @&(~1)salt pork{} with @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced) for ~sweat{6%min}.

>> step: simmer covered 1 hr 10 min
Simmer @&(~1)pork base{} covered with @dried lima beans{1%lb}(450 g; soaked overnight), @ham hock stock{2%qt}(1.9 L), @bay leaf{1}, @black pepper{1%tsp} for ~simmer{70%min}.

>> step: butter and salt at the end
Stir @&(~1)beans{} with @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(42 g), @kosher salt{2%tsp}.

Mash a ladleful against the side of the pot and stir it back in if the liquid is still thin.
